.TH CHANTEST 1
.SH NAME
chantest, raisetest \- diagnostics for the Dis virtual machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chantest
.PP
.B raisetest
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are diagnostics rather than smoke tests: each exists to answer one
question about the virtual machine, and each is meant to be run on a
kernel and compared against hosted
.IR emu (1).
.PP
.I Chantest
exercises channel and
.B alt
semantics \(em send and receive, buffered and unbuffered, several arms
ready at once, a channel closed under a waiting process.  It was written
before the per-channel locking of
.B doc/dis-parallel-plan.ms
rather than after it.  With one interpreter every case passes trivially;
the point is to have them passing beforehand, so that "still passes"
means something once more than one processor runs Dis.
.PP
.I Raisetest
asks whether a Limbo
.B raise
from inside a spawned process reaches the exception handler immediately
surrounding it.  Under hosted
.I emu
it does, and the program prints
.B "received caught"
and exits.  On a native kernel it did not: the marker printed and the
virtual machine went silent forever.  It is kept because a program that
reproduces an open bug is worth more than a note saying the bug exists,
and because the answer is expected to change.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/chantest.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/raisetest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR emu (1),
.IR prog (3)
.SH BUGS
Neither prints a summary line; read the output.
